\v 2 \vp 2138\vp* ’i ——— ’in ———
\c 744
\cp 693
\p
\v 1 \vp 2139\vp* To say: Awa[ke] ——— ḫnti n.k[m?] ———
\q1 ———
\v 2 \vp 2140\vp* the bows bend their head to thee, go[ing] from thee between (?) ———
\q1 ———
\v 3 \vp 2141\vp* the gods rejoiced; exult ———
\q1 ——— [he?] sees ———
\q1 ——— [Geb], prince of the gods
\v 4 \vp 2142\vp* he has taken the heritage; [he has] carried off
\q1 ———N ———
\v 5 \vp 2143\vp* Equip thyself with his white crown; eat bread
\q1 ——— [wi]th a presentation
\c 745
\cp 694
\p
\v 1 \vp 2144\vp* ——— says Isis; "I have found (him)," says Nephthys,
\q1 when they saw Osiris on his side on the shore [of Ndi.t]
\v 2 \vp 2145\vp* ——— rise up ———
\q1 ——— my brother, I sought thee;
\q1 raise thyself up, spirit." Geb said:
\q1 "I have smitten ——— the [Enn]ead
\v 3 \vp 2146\vp* ——— for thy father Atum,
\q1 that he may cause thee to be (on) the ḥnti-ocean among the gods,
\q1 as the Great One who is before ———
\q1 ———
\v 4 \vp 2147\vp* Those who are in Nun come to thee; mankind (the blessed dead (?)) circulate for thee;
\q1 thou art like Horus ———
\v 5 \vp 2148\vp* ——— with him, in thy time.
\q1 Thine annual (offerings) are made with him, in his hour,
\q1 by order of ———
\v 6 \vp 2149\vp* ———
\q1 The way of N. is open for N.; the way of N. is made (prepared?).
\v 7 \vp 2150\vp* N ———
\q1 ——— chief of the two lands.
\q1 N. is Thot chief of heaven; N. is Anubis chief of the house.
\v 8 \vp 2151\vp* It was brought, open ———
\q1 ——— to N., before N.
\v 9 \vp 2152\vp* He is the bittern (śdȝ-bird), which comes from the marsh
\q1 ———
\v 10 \vp 2153\vp* ———
\q1 who is in tnw of the four tnw, depart from N.
\v 11 \vp 2154\vp* N ———
\q1 N ———
\q1 pure is the tongue which is in the mouth of N.
\v 12 \vp 2155\vp* Protect N ———
\q1 ——— N ———
\q1 ——— that N. may not be upside down.
\v 13 \vp 2156\vp* N. is the bull ———
\q1 N. is the bull ———
\q1 three in heaven; two on earth.
\c 746
\cp 695
\p
\v 1 \vp 2157\vp* To say: The diadem comes into being; inundated ——— ti
\q1 tm ———
\v 2 \vp 2158\vp* Seat thyself on the throne of Rē‘, which Horus, removed to the south of the sky.
\q1 removed ——— fḫ (?) ———
\q1 ——— he removed the secret (places) of the Nine (Bows?).
\v 3 \vp 2159\vp* N. is seated ———
\q1 ——— n.f nb ———
\q1 ——— N. upon the sky.
\q1 The two hands of N. are on Heliopolis.
\v 4 \vp 2160\vp* ——— rd.wi [N.] ———
\q1 ——— ’ir.ś
\q1 the head of N. is above; the legs of N. [are below].
\v 5 \vp 2161\vp* [N.] ———
\q1 ——— more long than wide;
\q1 behold N. św t[ȝ?] ———
\v 6 \vp 2162\vp* ——— śšm ———
\q1 like to her following of Set; like to her foll[owing] ———
\q1 ——— m ——— ’i ———
\c 747
\cp 696
\p
\v 1 \vp 2163\vp* O, strong one, jackal, Dḳḳ, bring these to [this] N.;
\q1 bring with these to N ———
\q1 messenger of Atum, O N., with linen of Tȝ(?)i.t
\v 2 \vp 2164\vp* ———
\q1 O! O! come; O! O! come; bring these to N.;
\v 3 \vp 2165\vp* bring with (these) to N ———
\q1 lift him up ———
\q1 messenger of Atum, O N., with linen of Tȝ(?)i.t
\v 4 \vp 2166\vp* ——— the eye of Horus there
\q1 hurry against the fingers of Set
\q1 dȝ (or, wdȝ) ——— ’in(f) m—ś—
\v 5 \vp 2167\vp* ——— N. earth in peace
\q1 the two hands of N. ——— to the heart
\v 6 \vp 2168\vp* Raise thyself up N., tsi ———
\q1 N. raised himself up in this night ———
\q1 n these of N ———
\q1 ḥtm (?) ——— Šśȝ ———belonging to the god
\q1 O N. ———
\q1 63 ——— ’im-n.n ———
\q1 ——— he[aven] ———
\c 748
\cp 697
\p
\v 1 \vp 2169\vp* To say: O N., the mouth of the earth opens for thee; Geb speaks to thee:
\q1 "Thou art great like a king; thou art mighty like Rē‘.
\v 2 \vp 2170\vp* Thou purifiest thyself in the lake of the jackal; thou cleansest thyself in the lake of the Dȝt."
\q1 "Come in peace," say the Two Enneads to thee.
\q1 The eastern door of heaven is open for thee by ’Imn-kȝm.
\v 3 \vp 2171\vp* Nut has given her arms to thee, N., she of the long hair, she of the hanging breasts;
\q1 she lifts thee high to herself to heaven; she did not cast N. down to the earth.
\v 4 \vp 2172\vp* She gives thee birth, N., like S'ȝh;
\q1 she makes thee remain as chief of the two ’itr.t-palaces."
\q1 N. descends into the boat like Rē‘, on the shores, of the Winding Watercourse.
\v 5 \vp 2173\vp* N. is transported by the indefatigables;
\q1 N. commands the imperishable stars;
\q1 N. is transported on the ḥnti-ocean;
\q1 N. takes the helm to the fields of ḫȝḫȝ.
\v 6 \vp 2174\vp* Thy messengers go; thy runners hasten.
\q1 They say to Rē‘: "Behold, N. is come; behold, N. is come in peace."
\v 7 \vp 2175\vp* Do not go by these water-courses of the west;
\q1 those who go there, they do not come back.
\q1 Go thou, N., by these water-courses of the east,
\q1 among the Followers of [Rē‘]
\q1 ——— him who lifts up the arm in the east.
\q1 ———
\c 749
\cp 698
\p
\v 1 \vp 2176\vp* N ——— N. pw ———
\q1 mdś ntr.w m ———
\v 2 \vp 2177\vp* ——— śki
\q1 flesh; protect thyself; give way from behind N.
\c 750
\cp 699
\p
\v 1 \vp 2178\vp* ———
\q1 ——— Anubis, he lays hold of thine arm; Nut, she gives to thee thy heart.
\v 2 \vp 2179\vp* Thou fleest cloudlike as a falcon; thou drawest thyself out of the water like a nwr-bird;
\q1 thou goest towards the west ———
\v 3 \vp 2180\vp* ———
\q1 ——— [thou livest], thou livest; thou art young, thou art young;
\q1 to the side of thy father, to the side of Śȝḥ, to heaven.
\v 4 \vp 2181\vp* Thou livest ———
\q1 ———
\q1 ———
\c 751
\cp 700
\p
\v 1 \vp 2182\vp* To say: Father N.,
\q1 raise thyself up on thy right side; support thyself on thy left side.
\q1 Thy flesh has been collected for thee ———
\q1 ———
\v 2 \vp 2183\vp* ——— with which thou art pure as a god.
\q1 The messengers of Rē‘ come forth for thee; the imperishable stars take thine arm.
\q1 [Thou] diest not ———
\v 3 \vp 2184\vp* ———
\q1 [like Anubis] who is in Tȝḫb.t.
\v 4 \vp 2185\vp* Thy wȝg (offering) is of bread; wȝg is like the eye of Horus,
\q1 in (his) name of "Wȝg-(offering)."
\q1 Thy presentation ———
\q1 ———
\v 5 \vp 2186\vp* ——— thine enemies are destroyed; they perish;
\q1 they foam in opposing thee; throw them in the lake; throw them in the sea.
\v 6 \vp 2187\vp* Men come to thee ———
\q1 ———
\q1 ———
\c 752
\cp 701
\p
\v 1 \vp 2188\vp* To say: The Great One is fallen in Ndi.t; Isis is loosed from her burden (tn).
\q1 Raise thyself up, thou who art in Ntrw; raise thyself up
\v 2 \vp 2189\vp* ———
\q1 ——— the god is loosed.
\v 3 \vp 2190\vp* Horus comes forth from Chemmis;
\q1 Buto arises for Horus; he purifies himself there.
\v 4 \vp 2191\vp* Horus comes purified, that he may avenge [his father]
\q1 ———
\v 5 \vp 2192\vp* [I am thy sister], who loves thee, says Isis, says Nephthys.
\q1 They weep for thee; they awake for thee.
\v 6 \vp 2193\vp* O N., raise [thyself] up ———
\q1 ———
\v 7 \vp 2194\vp* ———
\q1 [(receive) thy thousand (loaves) of bread], [thy thousand (mugs) of beer], thy thousand cattle, thy thousand geese,
\q1 a roast, a double-rib piece from the slaughtering-bench of the god; the great bread and the rtḥ-bread from the broad-hall.
\v 8 \vp 2195\vp* Provide thyself, N., with ———
\q1 ———
\v 9 \vp 2196\vp* Thou hast thy wrr.t-crown; the wrr.t-crown is on thy head;
\q1 thou hast taken the wrr.t-crown before the Two Enneads
\q1 Thou art a spirit among [thy] brothers ———
\v 10 \vp 2197\vp* ———
\q1 ——— spirits.
\v 11 \vp 2198\vp* O N., stand up;
\q1 sit thou before thy heart like Anubis First of the Westerners.
\v 12 \vp 2199\vp* Thou art come (again) to [thy] (right) state ———
\q1 ———
\q1 ———
\c 753
\cp 702
\p
\v 1 \vp 2200\vp* To say: N. is come to you,
\q1 ye great and powerful pair of goddesses, who are on the eastern side of heaven,
\q1 that you both may carry N. and set him on the eastern side of heaven.
\c 754
\cp 703
\p
\v 1 \vp 2201\vp* To say: O. N., thy soul is with thee
\q1 ——— as Osiris.
\q1 O N., live, thou shalt not die.
\v 2 \vp 2202\vp* Horus comes to thee; he separates thy bandages; he casts off thy bonds.
\q1 Horus has expelled thy rivals,
\q1 the earth-gods seize thee not.
\v 3 \vp 2203\vp* O N., [thy] ka is mighty ———
\q1 Thy father is not among men; thy mother is not among mankind.
\v 4 \vp 2204\vp* Thy mother is the great ḥwr.t-uraeus, the white (crown), the royal head-dress, resident in el-Kâb,
\q1 she with variegated feather, she with the two hanging (and shaking) breasts.
\v 5 \vp 2205\vp* N. is not seized by ———
\c 755
\cp 704
\p
\v 1 \vp 2206\vp* To say: N. [is a male], coming forth from Rē‘;
\q1 N. has come forth from between the thighs of the Ennead;
\q1 Šsm.t.t conceived him; Šsm.t.t gave him birth;
\q1 N. is a falcon coming forth from Rē‘;
\q1 [N. is the living ’i‘r.t-serpent], which came forth from the eye of Rē‘;
\q1 he flies, he hovers over the throne of Khepri, in the bow of his boat in the sky.
\c 756
\cp 705
\p
\v 1 \vp 2207\vp* thy father ———
\c 757
\cp 706
\p
\v 1 \vp 2208\vp* ——— [in his name] of Rē‘.
\q1 N. was nursed on the milk (of) ———
\q1 ——— your arm.
\c 758
\cp 707
\p
\v 1 \vp 2209\vp* ——— his mother;
\q1 his mother is Šś3.t-Śti.t (Satis); guide ———
\q1 ———
\c 759
\cp 708
\p
\v 1 \vp 2210\vp* ——— one ———
\q1 ——— N ———
\q1 ——— with the ‘bȝ-sceptre ———
\c 760
\cp 709
\p
\v 1 \vp 2211\vp* ——— the Name of N ———
\q1 ——— his beloved son, coming forth from ———
\q1 ——— N. being ———
\q1 ——— to exist ———
\c 761
\cp 710
\p
\v 1 \vp 2212\vp* ——— these gods ———
\q1 ——— says the priest of Rē‘ to [N.]
\q1 ——— of the gods, he satisfies the spirits.
\q1 ——— N. the sky with ———
\q1 ——— his pellet of incense is broken ———
\v 2 \vp 2213\vp* Horus has put his arm around [N.] ———
\q1 ——— before N. N ———
\q1 ——— N. with natron ———
\q1 Thou art Thot who avenges it; thou art not [ like Set who took it].
\q1 ———
\c 762
\cp 711
\p
\v 1 \vp 2214\vp* ———
\q1 Thou has seen the Delta ———
\q1 N. voyages there to the shore (of) ———
\q1 ——— N. separates ———
\q1 ———
\c 763
\cp 712
\p
\v 1 \vp 2215\vp* ——— behind N ———
\q1 ———
\c 764
\cp 713
\p
\v 1 \vp 2216\vp* ——— to attack ———
\q1 ——— N ———
\q1 ——— N ———
